----
{#architecture slip enter="~duration:0.5"}
----
> # Architecture

{#architecture-part-1}
> - The first step is recovering the game's CFG. It starts from a set of known entry points (including reset vectors, interrupt vectors, and the start of boot loader ROM and user code).
> - More entry points can be discovered dynamically by running the generated binary with `--profile` flag to record the encountered PC values and then recompiling with that profile.
> - Each basic block is lowered to LLVM IR and funnels through a single shared return dispatcher, which routes control flow between basic blocks.
> - The IR is then optimized and compiled using the existing LLVM backends.

{pause=architecture-part-1 up="~duration:0.5 architecture-part-1"}

